* Kerr resonator: a junction diluted by a parallel inductor.
*
* Half of the linear inductance is the junction, so the mode inherits a weak, almost
* pure Kerr nonlinearity (about 15 MHz per photon) that barely changes with photon
* number. A coherent state left alone in it turns into Schroedinger cats.

.title  Kerr resonator
.name   kerr_resonator

J1  1  0  EJ=60  EC=200
L1  1  0  EL=60
C1  1  0  EC=0.03

.options ext_basis=harmonic
.cutoff ext1 = 70
.levels 24
.end
